# macOS portability fixes for files touched by rexglue-local-changes.patch,
# plus the recompiled-guest-module loader fix, applied after it. Windows code
# fixes preserve Windows platform behaviour. The PPC memory-barrier backport
# corrects generated fences on every host; runtime diagnostics default off and
# their environment gate is enabled only on Apple platforms.
#
#   src/ui/game_ui_fonts.cpp: _fseeki64() is an MSVC CRT extension. POSIX
#   (macOS/Linux) uses fseeko() with a 64-bit off_t, matching the existing
#   rex::filesystem POSIX file backend.
#
#   CMakeLists.txt: rex_resolve_version() defaults SOURCE_DIR to
#   CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR. Consumed via add_subdirectory() (the documented REXSDK_DIR
#   flow), CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR is the game workspace, so git describe reads the
#   consumer's tags; a consumer tagged v1.0 trips the "floor is behind tag"
#   guard. Pin the version probe to the SDK tree.
#
#   cmake/rexglue_helpers.cmake: defensive fallback for the installed-SDK
#   branch that reads REXGLUE_MOLTENVK_ICD (only the config package defines it).
#   The in-tree failure seen here comes from the other branch (empty
#   REXGLUE_ROOT) and is fixed in the consumer, see
#   Installer/recomp-template/CMakeLists.txt; this keeps the same fallback for
#   any consumer that reaches this branch without the variable.
#
#   src/system/kernel_state.cpp: recompiled guest modules are registered by
#   their bare SDK target name (the codegen template emits projectName + "_" +
#   targetName). Windows' LoadLibrary appends ".dll" and searches the loader
#   path, so the bare name resolves the DLL staged next to the host. POSIX
#   dlopen treats the name as a literal filename and never rewrites it, so on
#   Apple the caller now rebuilds the real dylib name (lib<name>.dylib) and
#   anchors it at the executable folder. Explicit absolute/relative paths pass
#   through untouched; there is no search of arbitrary directories.
#
#   include/rex/platform/dynlib.h + src/core/dynlib_posix.cpp: expose
#   DynamicLibrary::last_error() and record the verbatim dlerror() text when a
#   POSIX dlopen fails, so the loader failure above reports the exact dyld
#   reason. The header change is inert on Windows (the member stays empty).
#
#   src/core/exception_handler_posix.cpp: when no installed handler consumes a
#   synchronous fault, the POSIX handler returned to the faulting instruction,
#   which macOS re-executes -> an unhandled guest access violation spun forever
#   at ~400% CPU and rotated the log at ~24 MB/s. Windows returns
#   EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH and lets the default crash handling terminate the
#   process; restore the pre-install disposition and re-raise to match that.
#
#   src/core/threading_posix.cpp: retain sub-millisecond precision in macOS
#   multi-object timed waits. Alertable waits use 1 ms slices, whose remaining
#   time was truncated to zero, burning a core instead of sleeping. The runtime
#   benchmark in scripts/test-macos-wait-performance.sh covers the audio
#   worker's eight client semaphores and shutdown event; other platforms retain
#   their existing implementation. This is not an audio/playability fix claim.
#
#   src/codegen/builders/system.cpp: backport the fence mappings from upstream
#   bd833a2 (2026-10-02). The pinned generator discarded sync/lwsync/eieio
#   as x86 no-ops; ARM64 needs their ordering. A real decoder/writer
#   fixture fails all three barrier checks before this change. This is
#   a code-generation correctness fix, not proof of a gameplay speedup.
#
#   runtime diagnostics: RESTREET_PERF_DIAG enables an opt-in JSONL recorder
#   for audio starvation/content and shader/pipeline timings. The callback
#   only updates lock-free counters; a separate reporter writes once per
#   second. Software-only SDL tests cover enabled/disabled paths.
#
#   macOS presentation experiment: opt-in immediate host presentation leaves
#   guest vsync/readback policy intact; unavailable/prohibited immediate modes
#   preserve the normal fallback. Default remains disabled.
#
# Opt-in macOS idle achievement toast repaint suppression, with UI-thread
# notification delivery and weak lifetime cancellation; defaults off.
#
# Opt-in frame trace includes SDL/window paint triggers and UI/toast policy
# decisions to distinguish repeat-presentation sources; normal runs record none.
#
# macOS idle exit overlay: event-driven shortcut wake, UI-owned lifetime,
# opt-in repaint while open only; rebuild the consuming ReXApp executable.
# Vulkan shader/pipeline storage: rewind append-read files before header reads
# so Darwin reloads persisted cache entries instead of resetting both files.
# Audio content diagnostics distinguish numerical silence from non-silent
# repetitions and count invalid/out-of-range source samples; opt-in only.
#
#   src/core/clock.cpp + guest_clock_mapping.h: Mac-only anchored rational
#   guest clock preserves fractional ticks and avoids shared-mutex updates on
#   every read. Atomic coherent snapshots retain scalar, frequency, system-time
#   and uptime controls; config changes rebase under one writer mutex.
